    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9334" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνούσιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without substance,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲ ἄρα ἡ ἑτερότης ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dam.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					192
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ νεκροί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Procl.
					<u>in Alc.</u>
					p.271C.
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Olymp.
				<u>in Alc.</u>
				p.92C.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύναμις,</span> of God, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐσιώδης,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>Inst.</u>
				121
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Syrian.
					<u>in Metaph.</u>
					114.29
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in Alchemy,
				<i>not affecting substance, superficial in action,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σώματα</span> Zos.Alch.p <i><span class="en">
				160
			</span></i>B,al.</div>
